# §8 — size/usize machine-word types; memory positions reballed (byte-preserving)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT ENTERS (additive only; nothing removed — docs/design/mudancas-superficie-0.3.1.md §8):
#   - `PrimKind` (`src/checker/type.tks`) gains `Size` (signed) and `Usize` (unsigned), APPENDED
#     after `Bool` so every existing ordinal is stable (ordinal-safe for the `.tkb` prim tag, which
#     is the enum ordinal). `Size`/`Usize` are DISTINCT kinds from `uptr` (`Uptr`, the opaque FFI
#     address): a `usize` is a NUMBER that casts/does-arithmetic like `u64`; a `uptr` is a
#     transport-only opaque word. They are NOT unified.
#   - PREDICATES: `prim_is_int` (both true), `prim_is_signed` (`Size` true, `Usize` false),
#     `prim_width` (both 64), `numint_fits` (usize≡u64 range, size≡i64 range), `bignum_ctor_of`
#     (usize routes to `of_u64` like u64) — checker; `prim_is_signed_int`/`prim_width_of`/
#     `ltype_of_prim_name` — lir/lower; `prim_name` (surface spelling) — resolve.
#   - LEXER/RESOLUTION: `builtin_type` (`scope.tks`) resolves `size`→Prim{Size}, `usize`→Prim{Usize}
#     (type names are plain identifiers, so no lexer keyword table changes). The syntactic mirrors
#     `cg_te_to_type_ns`/`emit_type_expr`/`cg_is_builtin_scalar` (`codegen.tks`) recognize them too.
#   - LOWERING (prim → machine type, 64-bit): `Usize`→`uint64_t`, `Size`→`int64_t` in `emit_prim`;
#     the C-type/mangle/div-cast tables (`emit_type_expr`, `cg_opt_mangle`(_str), `prim_div_tag`,
#     `cg_int_width`) map both to their 64-bit twin so a `usize` typedef/helper is byte-identical to
#     `u64` (and `size` to `i64`). `ffi_export` (ffi_prim_name/ffi_c_scalar) and the native DWARF
#     base-type table (`dwarf.tks`) also learn them.
#   - `.tkb`: the reader `prim_of` (`tkb_read.tks`) now round-trips ordinals 11=`Size`/12=`Usize`;
#     the writer `prim_byte` (`k to byte`) emits them automatically. NO version bump — `src/` spells
#     no `size`/`usize`, so the EMITTED CORPUS carries no 11/12 byte and the wire does not actually
#     gain the ordinals here (`TKB_EXPR_VERSION`/`TKB_PROGRAM_VERSION` 4/6 stand). The reader accepts
#     them ahead of first use so a future reball round-trips without a compat break.
#   - SWEEP: NONE performed in `src/` (conservative). Every memory/collection `u64` the doc names
#     (slice `.len`/`.cap`, indices, offsets, the slice header) is part of a large connected
#     component that crosses `type_eq` STRICT boundaries (assignment to a `u64` slot, a `u64`
#     argument, a `u64` return) as the other type; because `Usize`≠`U64` at the type level, reballing
#     any single such position in isolation is REJECTED by the checker (not byte-different — it fails
#     to compile), and reballing an entire component atomically is exactly the broad, ambiguous class
#     §8's own conservatism directive says to leave alone. The infrastructure lands INERT; the reball
#     is deferred. NO runtime C touched.
#
